 "notes": "Diffraction-ready average R-3m B4C model in the conventional hexagonal setting. The atomic coordinates follow the Clark-Hoard/JCPDS average structure; split B/C occupancy on the polar icosahedral site gives exactly B36C9 in the cell. The lattice parameters a=5.601(1) A and c=12.087(5) A are the ambient sample values reported by Somayazulu et al. in the official supplement and give V=328.383 A^3, consistent with the fixed 328.4 A^3 EOS reference volume. Structure references: Clark and Hoard, J. Am. Chem. Soc. 65, 2115-2119 (1943), doi:10.1021/ja01251a026; Somayazulu et al. (2023), doi:10.1098/rsta.2022.0331; JCPDS/PDF 6-0555. PhaseSmith can expand the five asymmetric sites to calculate powder reflections and intensities.",
