   "fit_datasets": [
    "b4c_somayazulu_2023_table4_pvt"
   ],
   "notes": "Third-order Birch-Murnaghan reference isotherm plus Mie-Gruneisen-Debye thermal pressure. The room-temperature quench-data fit gives K0=221(2) GPa and K0'=3.3(1) with V0=328.4 A^3 fixed; those three reference parameters were then fixed in the P-V-T fit. The official supplement defines T0=298 K, theta0=1425 K, n=5 atoms per B4C formula unit, gamma(V)=gamma0*(V/V0)^q, and theta(V)=theta0*exp[(gamma0-gamma(V))/q]. With a=1, the paper's generalized Tange relation reduces exactly to this integrated constant-q MGD model. The final article reports gamma0=0.8 fixed and q=2.1 varied. At the 41 heated supplementary points' printed V and T, the published parameterization gives a pressure RMSE of 1.39 GPa and chi-squared per observation of 0.961. A Peritheos P-V-T errors-in-variables refit with gamma0 fixed gives q=1.050(519), so it does not independently recover q=2.1; details and the primary-data transcription are in docs/literature-reproductions.md. The average disordered R-3m structure is diffraction-ready and is reported stable over the experimental range.",
   "identifier": "b4c_somayazulu_2023_bm3_1",
   "pressure_calibration": {
    "status": "resolved",
    "methods": [
     {
      "kind": "equation_of_state",
      "reference": {
